    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0617" n="551" xml:id="pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/839: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-09T14:00:00-05:45">April 9, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. My 105, April 7, 4 p.m.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d542-f1"/> President informed
                    me this morning that he had appointed his brother Antioco Sacasa as Chief of
                    Staff of the Guardia in place of General Abaunza. Despatch by air mail.<anchor
                        n="62" xml:id="d542-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
